# Project videos

When adding or replacing a video on a project, follow this without asking the user to restate it.

## File

- **1920×1080**, 16:9, **MP4**, H.264, AAC stereo **128 kbps**.
- About **5 Mbps**. For a clip of roughly 1–2 minutes, land around **50–70 MB**. Stay **under 100 MB**.
- **Fast start** so playback can begin before the file finishes downloading.
- Strip location and other camera metadata. Leave the original file untouched and write a separate web file.

## Logo intro

- Open with a short logo card (**about 3 seconds**) on graphite `#333333`, using `public/brand/navbar-logo-v3-inverted.png` and a short gold `#C4973D` line under the lockup.
- Fade the logo in, then dissolve into the footage. The logo is not the thumbnail.

## On the project page

- One video section only, in this order: featured image, description, **Videos from this job**, then photo thumbnails. Do not add a second video block higher on the page.
- Keep each video card at the existing size: **`h-64`** inside `grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3`. Do not stretch a single video to full width.
- Set the Sanity video **Thumbnail** (`poster`) to a still from the footage (after the logo) that shows the work, with alt text. That still is the card image only.
- Do not set that still as the player `poster`. Playback starts on the logo.
- Keep the file URL in the page HTML and emit `VideoObject` (name, description, thumbnail, upload date, content URL) so the clip can be indexed.
